{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"07305e6366c18369","name":"card_event_cruiser_scouts","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/OceaniaStorm/events/card_event_cruiser_scouts","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CRUISER SCOUTS","text":"Pin a unit and Forecast. Also Intel 3 if you have 0 kredits.","flavorText":"Cruiser scouts were the eyes of the Imperial Japanese Navy’s long range task forces. Since Japanese carrier aircraft were usually kept for attack missions, much of the search work fell to floatplanes carried by cruisers. These aircraft were launched by catapult, then recovered from the sea after landing near their ships. The Tone class cruisers, Tone and Chikuma, were especially suited to this role. Their main guns were placed forward, leaving the stern free for a large aircraft-handling area. Chikuma could carry six floatplanes, giving the fleet a wider search screen. These scouts could shape an entire battle. Before the Pearl Harbor attack, Tone and Chikuma launched floatplanes for weather checks and patrols. In 1942 at Midway, their Aichi E13A floatplanes searched hundreds of miles for US ships. Chikuma’s aircraft later found USS Yorktown and shadowed her for hours. Cruiser scouts gave commanders vital information, but delays, mistakes, and fragile communications could turn even successful sightings into missed chances.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["ability.forecast"],"Name":"card_event_cruiser_scouts","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_cruiser_scouts_title","SourceString":"CRUISER SCOUTS","LocalizedString":"CRUISER SCOUTS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_cruiser_scouts_text","SourceString":"Pin a unit and Forecast. Also Intel 3 if you have 0 kredits.","LocalizedString":"Pin a unit and Forecast. Also Intel